(*
porta space-sync — A WRONGLY KINDED goal/liveness IS A LOG LINE, NOT A CRASH
(rete#231 D2), and `peekCell:ifStream:` is why.

`porta put --raw --kind stream` is a legal write, kind is pinned by the first write
and re-created by replay, and a bare `peek:` would raise 'not a cell' here on EVERY
tick forever — a raise that protectedFire: catches by ABANDONING the rest of the
reaction, so obs/health and tel/log would silently stop while the exchange kept
working. #180 and #206 are this same failure at a different path, and each one hung
a node at every boot until the row was found by hand.

Its own file because one image is one space: 19_liveness_goal.nsl pins this leaf as
a CELL, and `out:` raises on a cell.

expect:
stream is a log line true
node kept its own budget true
*)
class LivenessGoalStream packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | b |
    b:: platform PortaBridge socket: nil space: platform space id: 'test' peer: '::1' port: 1
        spans: platform Spans new timers: platform timers.
    b liveness: 2000 misses: 8.
    (platform space channel: 'goal/liveness') out: '' value: 'nonsense'.
    b applyLivenessGoal.
    ('stream is a log line ' , (b budMs = 16000) printString) println.
    (* And the node is still running: the send returned, nothing was abandoned. *)
    b applyLivenessGoal.
    ('node kept its own budget ' , (b budMs = 16000) printString) println.
  )
) : (
)
